WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Three actions have utilities zero, one and two. Each initially has probability one third.

00:06.000 --> 00:12.000
Conditioning on utility one with Gaussian label noise of standard deviation one favors the middle action.

00:12.000 --> 00:17.000
Utilities zero and two are equally far from the requested value. Both receive probability 0.274.

00:17.000 --> 00:23.000
Contrast conditions one and zero, with guidance weight one and label noise standard deviation one.

00:23.000 --> 00:28.000
The resulting target weights are proportional to exp(A): approximately 0.090, 0.245 and 0.665.

00:28.000 --> 00:33.000
Expected utility rises from 1 to 1.575. This illustrates exact normalized weights, not a neural sampler or benchmark.
